    feat(native): online-norm inputs in the streaming Predictor
    
    Predictor(online_norm=True) appends causal per-sequence z-scores of the
    raw row (n_in 323), matching build_inputs for --online-norm runs. Running
    sums are float32 in row order: CUDA cumsum along T is a sequential float32
    loop, so this reproduces the training-time features; f64 sums would shift
    outputs by up to 2.7e-2 (row group 1). Parity on ab25_onlinenorm: max
    1.8e-6 on rows >= 99; engine cost +1-3 us/row.
    
    package_submission.py flags online-norm members in members.json, rejects
    models the engine cannot run, and takes --native; build_native.sh holds
    the scorer docker build; parity_native.py measures parity and latency.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

